Split gehennom into three branches, lawful, chaotic, and neutral,
with Vlad & Candle, Rodney & Book, and vibrating square randomly
shuffled among the bottom level of each branch.

Then each branch of hell can pose different challenges, and all
of them could be shorter, may be only ten levels deep.

The chaotic branch could be mazes, as now, plus a random
six from ten demon lords plus court. That is, each demon lord
is accompanied by a few powerful monsters appearing only in
their lair; Orcus gets shade wizards, Jubilex gets shoggoths, etc.
They should be gauged to challenge players even with a full
ascension kit.

The lawful branch would be similar but with a different
selection of demon lords, gnomish mines style caverns
rather than mazes, ice traps instead of fire, etc.

The neutral branch could have normal room and corridor layout,
plus any six quest nemesis, in their normal lair but without
the quest artifacts, and probably with a souped-up retinue -
all those minions who died attacking the quest home level.

Demon lords and quest nememeses could resurrect, say 1% chance
per hundred turns, even if no corpse is left, so when you're
on your way up with the amulet there's a decent chance some
of them will ambush you, rather than you simply running through
empty lairs.

That would certainly more gehennom more varied, and probably
more challenging.

